1. The graph has a local maximum at approximately \(x=-2.5\), where it changes from rising to falling.
2. It has a local minimum at approximately \(x=0.75\), where it changes from falling to rising.
3. Therefore:

\[
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
\text{Increasing on }&(-\infty,-2.5)\cup(0.75,\infty),\\[2mm]
\text{Decreasing on }&(-2.5,0.75).
\end{aligned}}
\]
